{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: grid view lost upon rotation. Is that a bug in this app build? It might be the app's normal behavior (grid mode stored in per-activity viewpager). Hmm.\n\nAlso note the navigation drawer is open in landscape and obscures the left part; but main list still visible. In landscape, perhaps the drawer is in \"locked open\" mode by design? Amaze has a preference \"remember drawer\" / lock drawer. Hmm. Not sure.\n\nThis rotation-resets-grid issue is a candidate bug: \"directory view option not persisted on rotation\". But is it in scope \"sorting and directory view options\"? Yes, device rotate check is explicitly requested. However, it's possible in landscape the app deliberately uses list mode. Let's test: in portrait grid on, rotate to landscape → list. Rotate back → still list (menu says Grid View). So the setting is lost permanently. That's a genuine state bug.\n\nBut wait, maybe the menu label \"Grid View\" always refers to the action to switch to grid, regardless current mode? Check: when in grid mode, open menu—wait, earlier I enabled grid view, then rotated. In grid mode I didn't open the menu. Hmm, the label might be static \"Grid View\" meaning a toggle action that says \"Grid View\" even when already grid? Let me test: currently list view. I opened menu when in list and it said \"Grid View\". If I toggle to grid and open menu, if it still says \"Grid View\", it's static and not an indicator. Then rotation reset still confirmed by layout content (FrameLayout vs RelativeLayout), which is a reliable indicator. In landscape after rotate we saw RelativeLayout list items = list view. So yes grid lost.\n\nLet me continue testing other things; maybe report this later. But consider whether the app intentionally switches to list in landscape... Let's check by rotating while in grid view in a different folder, e.g., test twice. I did once. To reproduce reliably: rotate portrait → grid on in portrait → rotate landscape: list. Rotate back portrait: list. It reproduced twice (first time grid was on before rotating; second time also). Actually first time: I enabled grid at Amaze root, rotated, saw list, rotated back, saw list. Second time: enabled grid again (after rotation back), rotated, saw list. Yes reproducible twice.\n\nHowever, could it be that landscape always uses list? Then rotate back should restore grid if state retained. It doesn't. So state loss is real.\n\nI'll report this as a bug: Grid view option not preserved across rotation. But let's hold and continue testing more areas; maybe it's expected behavior in the app version. Hmm, risk of false positive. Let me think about Amaze v3.11.3 behavior. Amaze stores grid view state in a per-tab \"listViewMode\" in MainFragment? I recall Amaze has \"Grid View\" option in overflow per tab, and it likely is saved in SharedPreferences (per path?). Actually in Amaze, `MainFragment` uses `utils.setListOrGrid` stored in preferences. Hmm. If it were in SharedPreferences, rotation wouldn't reset.\n\nWait, another thought: maybe the rotation caused the app to restart and it loaded a different tab or reset to list because \"list view\" mode applied only to the current tab session. Regardless, as a QA finding, state lost on rotate is reportable.\n\nBut before reporting, let me also test whether leaving the folder and returning preserves grid mode (maybe it resets too). That's another state check. In portrait, let's rotate back, enable grid, navigate into Alpha, back, and see.\n\nLet me rotate back first."}
