{"type": "thinking", "text": "Type descending: txt first, then jpg. Within groups, order is descending by... report before notes (report 13B < notes 15B) hmm, that's not size desc nor name desc? report+final < notes alphabetically? \"notes\" < \"report\" ascending, so descending would be report then notes — yes consistent with name descending! And jpg: photo then keep descending name (photo > keep). Interesting! So the ties are broken by name descending because direction desc applies to name as tiebreak? Maybe comparator: type then name? In asc case: keep.jpg then photo.jpg (name ascending: keep < photo) and notes then report (name ascending). Yes! That's exactly consistent: within type, name ascending for asc; name descending for desc. Great, Type sort is correct.\n\nNow test Sort By Last Modified. Files all same timestamp Nov 14 7:13 AM, so order may be name asc/desc. Not very meaningful. Skip? Could test folders. Eh.\n\nTest \"Only this folder\" checkbox: This affects global sort setting. When checked, only current folder's sort applied. Hard to verify, but can test that with checked + sort type name asc in Alpha, then navigate to Amaze and see previous sort remains. However complexity. The task list says sorting and directory view options; I've covered main.\n\nOne more key thing: sort direction persisted; verify leave and come back. Already verified name desc persisted through navigation and rotation. Good.\n\nNow: paste conflict tests more thoroughly. We tested apply-to-all skip. Need to test \"Do for all items\" with OVERWRITE and RENAME maybe. But the build change says checkbox kept for remaining items. Maybe there's a bug: checkbox state not retained when it's unchecked and choosing SKIP for first then the second dialog appears (checkbox should be unchecked / respected). Let's test: copy two files into Alpha where both exist; paste; in first dialog leave checkbox unchecked; choose SKIP. Second dialog should appear for the other file. If second dialog appears, fine. Then choose SKIP too.\n\nAlso test OVERWRITE: copy two files with modified content? Hard to verify contents. We can check file sizes maybe. Overwrite with the same content from same source = same. Not verifiable easily. But we can verify no duplicates and count stays 3.\n\nMaybe more valuable: test rename-on-conflict (RENAME) with the checkbox? If \"Do for all items\" checked and RENAME chosen, does it prompt for new name for each? Let's see. If buggy, might rename both to same name or only first. Hmm. Let me test rename dialog on conflict: copy notes.txt into Alpha (conflict), choose RENAME → should show rename dialog with suggested \"notes (1).txt\". Then save → verify new file. Then delete it to restore.\n\nLet's first do the unchecked-SKIP second-dialog test.\n\nRecopy: go up to Amaze, copy both, into Alpha, paste.\n\nActually I'm in Amaze now. Long press notes.txt (11), tap report (17), copy, tap Alpha... but Alpha position now 21/24 depends. Let me just do it.\n\nActually, we can avoid repeated copying by noting the paste snackbar persists only after copy. Fine.\n\nLong press notes element 11."}
