serve is quick. It didn't show. Hmm, likely the app shows an error snackbar? We may have missed it. I'll retest.)\n- [x] copy single file to folder\n- [x] copy multiple files, conflict skip, apply-all skip, rename\n- [ ] cut file to folder and move back\n- [ ] copy folder\n- [ ] rename folder\n- [ ] paste conflict overwrite (maybe skip)\n- [ ] verify no duplicate entries after operations\n\nBookmarks:\n- Add bookmark for current dir; verify appears in bookmarks list\n- Add duplicate bookmark (same title/location) → should reject (new comparison on title+location)\n- Add bookmark with same title different location and same location different title → should be allowed (the change means comparing both title and location). Important: test that same title + different location is allowed, and different title + same location allowed.\n- Edit/delete bookmark?\n- Persistence after restart.\n\nNetwork SMB:\n- Add SMB connection; check Anonymous checkbox greys out username/password fields.\n- Uncheck → fields editable.\n- Test empty values, invalid, etc.\n- Verify connection dialog validation.\n- Also maybe FAB \"Cloud Connection\".\n\nLet me get to bookmarks/network soon. But first finish copy/paste/rename.\n\nTest cut: from Alpha, cut notes.txt (one of the pasted extras) and paste into Beta. Then later delete it. Let's do it.\n\nActually better to use the extra files we need to delete anyway. Cut Alpha/notes.txt → Beta/Renamed? Then cut back? No need since we'll clean up. But we should verify cut removes from source and appears in destination.\n\nSteps: long press notes.txt in Alpha (14). Tap Cut. Navigate up (BACK) to Amaze, tap Beta (position 23), then snackbar PASTE. Verify Beta contents: readme.txt + notes.txt. Then go back and delete notes.txt from Beta.\n\nLet's do it."}
