ECKED, fill connection name and hostname, username empty → CREATE → observe. If a connection gets created with anonymous enabled automatically without user action, that's odd. But maybe expected: app treats empty username as anonymous. The star (*) indicates required, so validation should complain. But it didn't and instead silently changed anonymous. Hmm.\n\nActually wait — maybe the checkbox was reset to checked by a config change? Did the keyboard hide trigger activity recreation? No.\n\nHmm, but note that when I pressed BACK to hide keyboard, the observation showed Anonymous not checked (element 7 no checked). Then tapped CREATE at (875,1990). Immediately after, the screen returned to file list for 3s (we observed file list), then after wait, the dialog re-appeared with Anonymous checked and DELETE/UPDATE. \n\nMaybe the actual flow: CREATE saved the connection AND started a network connection task; when it failed... no.\n\nCould the dialog with DELETE/UPDATE be a *new* dialog opened automatically because the connection was created and app wants you to verify? Hmm. But then why Anonymous checked? Because the save might treat empty username as anonymous and persist anonymous=true; when re-opening, it displays anonymous checked. But why reopen at all?\n\nWait! Maybe the file list we saw was the app after CREATE, and the re-appearing dialog was because my earlier tap on \"SMB Connection\" row (from drawer?) No, I tapped CANCEL after. Hmm, actually sequence: tap CREATE → observe showed file list (dialog closed) → wait 3s → observe showed dialog with DELETE/UPDATE. So the dialog reopened by itself after 3s. That's likely the app's \"edit connection\" screen appearing after successful creation (maybe it auto-opens when connection fails?).\n\nHmm, maybe the CREATE triggered a connection attempt; upon failure, the app reopens the edit dialog with an error toast. But no error text. The re-opened dialog had DELETE/UPDATE (edit mode) and Anonymous checked, meaning it was showing the saved connection (with anonymous true). But why would anonymous be true? Because username empty → maybe SMB library sets anonymous.\n\nThis could be \"expected\": For an SMB connection, if no username, anonymous. But the required * marker suggests otherwise.\n\nI think there's a more clear bug: the username field is marked required (*), but CREATE accepted it empty (dialog closed, connection saved) with no validation error. However, the anonymous checkbox auto-checked could be the app's intent: if username is empty, anonymous. But then the required marker is misleading. Hmm, may be a design choice.\n\nLet me reproduce carefully with username filled to see CREATE behavior: fill username \"test\" password \"x\", hostname dummy → CREATE → probably shows \"connection failed\" error. That would be good to verify.\n\nBut first delete this connection. Tap pencil 20 (edit for SMB Connection row 19)."}
