{"type": "thinking", "text": "Connection name validation shows \"Connection name cannot be empty\". Good. So connection name required validated.\n\nCancel this dialog (CANCEL) to avoid changes; but we need to delete the added connection anyway. Actually current edit-mode dialog is for the saved connection. Cancel, then delete via drawer pencil.\n\nWait, the anonymous auto-check behavior: is it truly automatic? Let me look: The dialog reopened in edit mode because... maybe the CREATE click triggered the save and the app navigated into the connection (SMB) which then failed, and re-opened the edit dialog? Hmm.\n\nConsider that maybe \"SMB Connection\" default connection name equals an existing connection name? No, we deleted the previous one. After deletion the connection list should be empty. Hmm.\n\nOK here's a thought: maybe the CREATE tap didn't actually happen in create mode. Perhaps the app re-renders the dialog after an async SMB scan returns and flips into edit mode... unlikely.\n\nLet me look at whether the app shows a connection error message when tapping CREATE with anonymous checked: Now in edit mode, tap UPDATE. It will save and close (as before). No connection attempt? Hmm.\n\nI think the auto-anonymous is likely intended: In Amaze's SmbConnectionDialog (I vaguely recall), when username is empty, it sets anonymous. But then why is the dialog reopened? Maybe reopening is the bug — but is it? Let me test whether it's actually automatic reopening after CREATE or something else. After tapping CREATE, immediately it showed edit mode (this time the observation right after CREATE showed edit mode; earlier there was a 3s delay showing file list first). This time the response was immediate (dialog edit mode). So CREATE → immediately transition to edit mode? That seems like the app's dialog stays (reuses same dialog) and switches buttons to UPDATE/DELETE after saving? Weird.\n\nActually maybe the flow is: tapping CREATE validates and starts the \"create connection\" process; upon success the dialog is dismissed and a new dialog opens because... no.\n\nHmm. It could be that an SMB connection with \"anonymous\" and hostname \"10.0.0.1\" triggered \"connection failed\" and the app re-opens the edit dialog to allow correction. But there's no error toast. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the re-opened dialog is a *new* \"SMB Connection\" creation dialog because tapping CREATE ... no, the buttons are UPDATE/DELETE, indicating edit existing.\n\nHmm, maybe the app opens \"Edit connection\" screen after creating a connection if you long-tap? no.\n\nWhatever the cause, it's confusing. Is it worth reporting? The user-visible defect could be: \"Tapping CREATE on an SMB connection with empty username silently saves it as anonymous (checkbox auto-checks) instead of showing the required-field error; the dialog then reopens in edit mode.\" A developer might reply \"Anonymous is auto-enabled when username empty — expected.\" Risky.\n\nLet me focus on clearer issues. Let me check the \"Paste conflicts Apply to all\" more: The task explicitly changed it; maybe there's still a bug. We tested SKIP apply-all. Let's test \"OVERWRITE\" apply-all with two files and \"RENAME\" apply-all. RENAME with apply-all is interesting: if \"Do for all items\" checked and RENAME chosen for first conflict, does it rename all? That likely would try to rename automatically with suggested names, without prompting. Could break (e.g., rename only first, or crash). Hmm.\n\nAlso test the conflict dialog checkbox \"Do for all items\" retained when the same paste has 3 conflicts and user unchecks after first? Hmm.\n\nAlso the changed bookmark behavior: tested duplicate prevented and same title diff location allowed. But there's another dimension: same location, different title — should be allowed (new entry compared on title+location). Can we test? The modify dialog only allows title change; adding by folder path only. Actually \"Add to Bookmarks\" for a file/folder directly adds with folder name as title. There's no way to change location in UI. But \"location\" might refer to the bookmark's \"path\" field in a different version. Our Modify dialog only has Name. Hmm.\n\nWait — maybe the \"Bookmarks page in Settings\" exists in a different screen where you can add a bookmark manually with title+location. Since Settings is unreachable so far, maybe I'm missing it. Let me find Settings. Perhaps it's accessible from Android's \"Settings\" app?? No.\n\nLet me search the app UI more systematically: Maybe Settings is at the bottom of the drawer after APKs, but hidden because the drawer is too tall and we need to scroll. My swipes on drawer didn't move. Maybe swiping up in the drawer area with x=400,y=1800 was interpreted on the *underlying file list* (since drawer transparent?) and scrolled nothing. But the drawer is a real view. Hmm.\n\nThe drawer elements list has APKs at y=2215, and screen height 2400. So if Settings items existed they'd be off-screen. The drawer list likely scrolls. Why didn't it? Possibly because the swipe gesture started on a clickable row (a LinearLayoutCompat clickable) which intercepted? Usually swipes on clickable rows still scroll in RecyclerView. But this looks like a plain LinearLayout/ScrollView. Let's try swipe from y=2300 to y=700 at x=300 (bottom blank area).\n\nOpen drawer now (currently in edit dialog; cancel first)."}
