FTP\" section? no.\n\nOK let me try long-press on the drawer \"Quick access\" item or on drawer blank space? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively — maybe the settings screen is accessible via the \"Cloud Connection\" FAB?? no.\n\nLet me try tapping the \"SMB Connection\" drawer row's pencil -> edit dialog; maybe there's an overflow in dialog? no.\n\nMaybe I should search the app's activities via \"Recent apps\" switch? No.\n\nPerhaps Settings is accessible from the launcher's app shortcut (long press app icon). Not through our tools (we can't see launcher shortcuts maybe). Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the app's \"Settings\" is accessible via the system notification or via the three-dot in the *file list* but our overflow is scrolled: The popup menu had 7 items and maybe more below (Exit at y=892, screen space plenty). No.\n\nLet's try swiping the overflow menu? It's a popup list; perhaps it has \"Settings\" below Exit, but the popup size fits. The popup ended at y≈940. No.\n\nCould there be a second page of overflow accessible by scrolling the popup? Unlikely.\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider: maybe this app build is \"Amaze Debug\" with hidden settings because it's a test harness; but the task says \"Bookmarks page in Settings\". Could be that Settings is a *dialog* opened by some menu, e.g., \"Set As Home\" etc. Not.\n\nLet me try the \"Add to Bookmarks\" from the toolbar overflow? no.\n\nMaybe bookmark additions in this app are done from \"Settings\" → but we reached \"Add to Bookmarks\" via context menu, and the modify bookmark dialog is what matters. Since the changed behavior (dedupe by title+location) is testable there, we've covered it. The \"Settings\" page might not be reachable in this build; that's okay as long as we test bookmarks.\n\nLet me test another aspect of bookmarks: persistence across app restart (Exit and reopen). Already exit/reopen earlier — bookmarks existed (we had added Alpha). Actually we added Alpha before exit? Timeline: added Alpha bookmark, then added Beta, renamed Beta to Alpha, then deleted both, then exit/open app happened *after* deletion? Let's see: We exited the app right after deleting the bookmarks? No—exit happened after we restored bookmarks? Sequence: add Alpha, duplicate test, add Beta, rename Beta→Alpha, duplicate test, tap Alpha row (second) → Beta, delete second, delete first, then... we explored drawer, tapped app_version, Home, more options, Exit → launcher → open_app. At that time bookmarks were deleted. So persistence of added bookmarks across restart wasn't verified.\n\nLet me re-add a bookmark, exit, reopen, verify it persists, then delete. That's a good state test. But maybe not necessary since SharedPreferences. Still, do it for thoroughness.\n\nActually we also need to clean the SMB connection. Let's do SMB cleanup first: drawer → pencil on SMB Connection → DELETE.\n\nCurrent state: search screen with keyboard maybe. Press back to exit search."}
