vice: portrait → landscape → portrait keeps grid layout.\"\nobserved: \"After enabling Grid View in portrait, rotating to landscape shows list layout, and rotating back to portrait still shows list layout; the overflow action reads 'Grid View' again.\"\nsteps: [\"Navigate to /storage/emulated/0/AndroidQA/Amaze\",\"Open overflow menu and tap 'Grid View' (file list switches to grid tiles)\",\"Rotate to landscape\",\"Rotate back to portrait\",\"Open overflow menu: it shows 'Grid View' again and the list is in list layout\"]\nobserved_quote: \"Grid View\"\nelement_ref: 2 (maybe).\n\nHmm, observed_quote \"Grid View\" is the action label shown after the revert; exact. Good.\n\nReport 2 (SMB):\nscreen: \"SMB Connection dialog (New cloud connection → SMB Connection → Enter hostname manually)\"\nelement: \"Anonymous checkbox / CREATE button\"\nsymptom_type: wrong_value\nexpected: \"With Anonymous unchecked, Username is marked required (*), so CREATE with an empty Username should show the required-field error and not save the connection.\"\nobserved: \"Tapping CREATE with Anonymous unchecked and Username empty saves the connection and silently turns the Anonymous checkbox on (username/password fields become disabled); no validation error is shown.\"\nsteps: [...]\nobserved_quote: \"Anonymous\"\nelement_ref: omit? Latest observation had no SMB dialog. Hmm, could include 7 from earlier SMB dialog observation but stale. I'll omit.\n\nReport 3 (rename pre-error):\nscreen: \"Rename dialog\"\nelement: \"Error message under the name field (textinput_error)\"\nsymptom_type: wrong_value\nexpected: \"The rename dialog opens clean, with no validation error until the user attempts to save an invalid name.\"\nobserved: \"Immediately on opening the Rename dialog, before any edit, it displays 'No changes were made as the new name matches the old name.' in red.\"\nsteps: [\"Navigate to /storage/emulated/0/AndroidQA/Amaze\",\"Tap the Properties/more icon next to notes.txt and choose Rename\",\"Observe the dialog immediately: the red error text is already displayed\"]\nobserved_quote: \"No changes were made as the new name matches the old name.\"\nelement_ref omit.\n\nShould I also report the stale count #3? Let me think about whether it's likely a real bug and confidently reproducible in principle. It appeared when the folder list was not re-queried after returning from the drawer. Specifically in Beta \"0 folders and 1 files\" changed to \"0 folders and 0 files\" while readme.txt listed. This is exactly the kind of \"consistency\" bug the task asks for. But we only saw it twice and couldn't reproduce on third attempt. Since the device died, I can't attempt a 4th time. Reporting without repro twice is against \"Reproduce a problem once before you report it\" — I observed it twice, so reproduction occurred. Actually the instruction says reproduce once before reporting; I've seen it twice. The third failure doesn't negate. But the steps are uncertain. I can report it with the observed quote \"0 folders and 0 files\" and the path. Hmm, but if dev can't repro, they may reject. The report's \"steps\" would be the observed sequence: open Beta, open drawer, close drawer, count goes 0/0. In my final test, that sequence did NOT reproduce. So steps not reliable. Skip.\n\nShould I report rename-to-existing silent no-op? Observed once. Not reproduced. Skip.\n\nLet me file the 3 reports. Actually, maybe just the two high-confidence: grid rotation and rename pre-error. The SMB one is 50/50. But the SMB area is in the test scope and the change, and there could be a genuine regression. Think harder.\n\nCould the behavior be explained as: The app auto-checks Anonymous when username is empty *on purpose* (some apps do). In that case the dialog re-opening as edit mode is a separate weird thing. Hmm, why did the dialog reopen at all? That's actually the bigger anomaly: after tapping CREATE, the dialog transitioned from Create mode to Edit mode without dismissing. Maybe the